================================================================================

Context: The graph-backend refactor (hats + factory-vended capabilities +
import boundary) had landed in code, the coding_rules inheritance table, and
`docs/backend.md`, but Cursor rules and Claude skills still described the
removed `GraphDBBackend` god-base. Agents adding a new engine would have
followed the stale pattern.

Changes:

1. .cursor/07-project-conventions.mdc
   Replace the `graphdb/` subpackage pattern with hats, capability accessors,
   and the cloisonnement rule; update the inheritance bullet.
2. .cursor/04-project-structure.mdc
   Note `interfaces/` plus cloisonned `lakebase`/`delta`/`neo4j` engines.
3. .cursor/08-testing-and-deployment.mdc
   Document that `test_backend_import_boundary.py` is zero-offender, not a
   shrinking baseline.
